I’ve just started a chat session in the interactive view of the Teich Studio UI. The previous step set the provider to “chat” and clicked the start button, which returned “started”. The UI now shows the chat interface, but I haven’t yet sent any message. To verify that the SSE (server‑sent events) pipeline is working end‑to‑end, I need to simulate a user typing a message into the composer input and hitting send. The UI should then attempt to call the backend; because there’s no API key configured, it will error, but that’s fine – I just need to confirm that the UI updates the status element appropriately, indicating that a request was made and that the SSE handling is wired.

The appropriate way to do this through the preview tools is to run a JavaScript expression in the browser context. I’ll locate the composer input element (`#composer-input`), set its `value` to a test string, then trigger the send button (`#btn-send`). After clicking, I’ll read the text content of the status element (`#chat-status`) which should reflect the current state (e.g., “Error: missing API key” or “Waiting…”). Returning that text will let me confirm the UI reacted as expected.

